Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: @DEPENDS@
Section: science
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/SatoruGoj0/Bonsai-Oryon
Description: ARM64 CPU inference engine for PrismML Ternary Bonsai (PQ2_0) models
 Bonsai Oryon is a CPU-only build of the PrismML fork of llama.cpp
 (pinned commit e3de715) with AArch64 NEON kernels tuned for the PQ2_0
 2-bit/ternary format used by Ternary-Bonsai-2-9B, intended for Qualcomm
 Snapdragon X (Oryon) laptops running Debian.
 .
 Provides bonsai-cli, bonsai-server (OpenAI-compatible HTTP API, bound to
 127.0.0.1 by default) and bonsai-bench. The CPU kernel variant is chosen at
 run time from the CPU's HWCAP flags (NEON, DOTPROD, FP16, I8MM, SVE...),
 so the package runs on any ARMv8-A CPU. All libraries are private
 (/usr/lib/bonsai-oryon) and never conflict with other llama.cpp installs.
 Model weights are not included.
